LumOn - Phase 22.X - Multi-ChunkSlot Surface Cache Support

Goal
- [ ] Enable proper multi-chunk surface cache addressing so many visible chunks can concurrently populate material/depth/irradiance tiles without aliasing (virtual address = chunkSlot + virtualPageIndex).

Non-goals (for this todo)
- [ ] Implement surface-cache mips (defer).
- [ ] Full UE5-Lumen card parity (defer; focus on chunk identity + page table correctness).


Phase 1 - Decide Slot Topology + Contracts
- [x] Decide whether the surface cache window is 2D (XZ) or 3D (XYZ) in chunk units.
- [x] Specify window dimensions in chunks (W×D or W×H×D).
- [x] Specify `originMinChunk` and ring offsets.
- [x] Define `chunkSlotCount` relationship to window dimensions.
- [x] Define deterministic mapping: `chunkCoord -> localIndex -> ring-wrapped chunkSlot`.
- [x] Define per-slot generation semantics (counter, wrap, stale rejection).
- [x] Decide where generation is encoded (PatchIdGBuffer.x high bits vs PatchIdGBuffer.w).
- [x] Write a short “CPU/GPU contract” note for chunkSlot + generation.
- [x] Decouple `chunkSlotCount` (page table layers) from physical pool `RequestedPages`/`CapacityPages`.


Phase 2 - PatchIdGBuffer: Encode Real chunkSlot (+ optional generation)
- [x] Add GLSL helper to compute `chunkCoord` from `worldPos` (chunk size 32).
- [x] Add GLSL helper `MapChunkCoordToSlot(chunkCoord, originMinChunk, ring, dims) -> chunkSlot`.
- [x] Update PBR chunk shader injection so PatchIdGBuffer emits real `chunkSlot` (and generation if used).
- [x] Keep existing voxel patchId mapping unchanged initially.
- [x] Update/extend debug GBuffer view(s) to visualize chunkSlot (+ generation).


Phase 3 - Feedback Dedup: Make Mark/Compact Multi-Slot
- [x] Replace single 128×128 stamp with per-slot stamp: `uimage2DArray vge_pageUsageStamp` sized 128×128×chunkSlotCount.
- [x] Update `lumonscene_feedback_mark_pages.csh`:
  - [x] Remove `chunkSlot!=0` early-out.
  - [x] Mark: `imageAtomicMax(stamp, ivec3(vx,vy,chunkSlot), frameStamp)`.
  - [x] If generation is enabled: reject mismatched generation.
- [x] Update `lumonscene_feedback_compact_pages.csh`:
  - [x] Dispatch over `(virtualPageIndex, chunkSlot)`.
  - [x] Output requests with real `chunkSlot`.
- [ ] Add bounded-request fairness:
  - [x] Choose strategy (per-slot budgets vs scan offset/round robin).
  - [x] Implement strategy and document expected behavior.


Phase 4 - CPU Residency + PageTable Mirrors: Key by (chunkSlot, vpage)
- [x] Update `LumonSceneFeedbackRequestProcessor`:
  - [x] Remove `chunkSlot==0` restriction.
  - [x] Key residency dictionaries by `(chunkSlot, virtualPageIndex)` (e.g. 64-bit packed key).
  - [x] Resize/reshape `pageTableMirror` to `[chunkSlotCount * VirtualPagesPerChunk]`.
  - [x] Ensure eviction clears correct page table slice.
- [x] Update `LumonSceneFeedbackUpdateRenderer`:
  - [x] Allocate mirrors based on configured `chunkSlotCount`.
  - [x] Read/process request batches across multiple slots.
  - [x] Make recapture bookkeeping slot-aware (or explicitly per-slot).


Phase 5 - Slot Lifecycle + Reuse Safety
- [x] Add slot assignment tracking: `chunkCoord -> chunkSlot` and reverse.
- [x] On reassignment:
  - [x] Clear page table slice for slot.
  - [x] Release/free physical pages associated with slot.
  - [x] Increment `slotGeneration[chunkSlot]`.
- [x] Ensure generation is GPU-visible (e.g. `ChunkSlotInfoBuffer`) and used for stale rejection.


Phase 6 - Capture + Relight: Provide Per-Slot Chunk Origins/Transforms
- [x] Add GPU buffer: `ChunkSlotInfoBuffer[chunkSlot]` containing:
  - [x] chunk origin (block units) or chunkCoord
  - [x] generation
  - [x] optional transform hooks for rotated blocks / mesh cards later
- [x] Update voxel capture compute to use chunkSlot info for world-space reconstruction (as needed).
- [x] Update voxel relight tracer to use chunkSlot info for ray origins/bounds (as needed).


Phase 7 - Tests: Multi-Slot + Multi-Frame Convergence
- [x] GPU tests (feedback):
  - [x] Multi-slot mark/compact produces requests for each slot without collisions.
  - [x] Bounded `vge_maxRequests` does not permanently starve higher slots (fairness test).
- [x] GPU tests (capture):
  - [x] Multi-slot capture writes distinct tiles for identical patchIds in different slots.
- [x] Integration test:
  - [x] “100 chunks visible” synthetic scene over N frames:
    - [x] Emit 100 chunkSlots worth of patch ids.
    - [x] Run mark→compact→CPU alloc→capture repeatedly under budget.
    - [x] Assert per-slot tile coverage grows over time (convergence).
- [x] Slot reuse tests:
  - [x] Generation increments and stale requests are rejected (GPU + CPU).


Phase 8 - Runtime Instrumentation + Debugging
- [x] Add LumonScene stats:
  - [x] requests by chunkSlot (top-k)
  - [x] skipped due to generation mismatch
  - [x] skipped due to per-slot budgets / fairness behavior
- [x] Add debug overlay(s):
  - [x] chunkSlot visualization
  - [x] optional page table occupancy heatmap per slot
